      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T06:18:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If its not too much big of a deal, then I\u0027d like to keep it how I have. The main reason is that I don\u0027t want to be handcrafting much of this. I typically make changes, and then simply run the auto formatter only to the lines modified by me (otherwise it ends up formatting the entire file). Now, I know that it creates a bit of inconsistency in the local code style, but I think its moving the needle in the right direction, coz it will prevent future developers writing code in this file to undo this piece of formatting every time they run auto formatter.",
      "parentUuid": "d51f58fb_6a54246e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1224,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1228,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "62cff1d1cae3a31bd6f91b8ccd3e40933f0720d9",
