      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T18:19:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think your computations are correct, but boy are they difficult to follow. It\u0027s none of your fault really, it\u0027s written as simply as possible (modulo inline comments), but the processing done here has enough variables that it\u0027s pretty confusing.\n\nCould you write some simple comments explaining what this does ? Something like :\n// Consider only entries that go onto the VPN interface.\n// In a first pass, reduce the values by however much the VPN managed to not\n// send over the wire out of what was written on the VPN interface : spread out\n// the wins evenly across UIDs.\n// In a second pass, distribute these values across interfaces in the proportion that\n// each interface represents of the total traffic of the underlying interfaces.\n\n(feel free to take wholesale, to correct or clarify stuff, or to reject wholesale and write something better)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1261,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 1261,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "62cff1d1cae3a31bd6f91b8ccd3e40933f0720d9",
