      },
      "lineNbr": 1300,
      "author": {
        "id": 1399364
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-22T06:18:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is to prevent divide by zero exception which can happen if no traffic sent by apps, but VPN app sent traffic of its own over underlying networks.\nMaybe using \"!\u003d\" is slightly better than \"\u003e\", but latter is more safe as it avoids negative stats, if at all that is possible (though extremely dangerous since it would easily go unnoticed). Also, I think for the same reason, the code on the left hand side had these checks.",
      "parentUuid": "a0497f04_b084a9d4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1300,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 1300,
        "endChar": 48
      },
